{
  "id": "Compound::DB00755 - Gene::5915",
  "verbalization": "Tretinoin is linked to Rarb through a shared pathway involving Acitretin, a metabolite of Tretinoin. The evidence suggests that Tretinoin causes various effects, including decreased night vision, hyperostosis, and decreased tolerance, all of which are mediated by Acitretin. Acitretin binds to Rarb, indicating a direct interaction between the compound and the target protein. The lowest common ancestor of these relationships is the Alpha, Beta-Unsaturated Monocarboxylic Acid, suggesting a common biochemical pathway. The consistent involvement of Acitretin as a mediator across different effects implies a general mechanism by which Tretinoin influences cellular processes through Acitretin-Rarb interactions. The evidence supports a role for Rarb in the biological effects of Tretinoin, though the specific molecular mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
